    {
      "id": "k4hlvfy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Energy is defined as the capacity to do work and is a scalar quantity.",
        "Kinetic Energy (KE = ½ mv²) depends directly on the mass and the square of velocity.",
        "Potential Energy (PE = mgh) is the stored energy of an object due to its height, position, or configuration.",
        "Mechanical Energy is the sum total of Kinetic Energy and Potential Energy of a system.",
        "Power is the rate at which work is done or energy is transferred (Power = Work / Time)."
      ],
      "id": "jwmt931"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mh4adqv",
      "content": "• Energy is the capacity to do work."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "roofn0j",
      "content": "• Energy can exist in different forms such as mechanical energy, heat energy, electrical energy and chemical energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1n3ruw7",
      "content": "• The SI unit of energy is Joule (J)."
    },
    {
      "id": "rw7sp60",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Forms of Energy"
    },
