    {
      "id": "x83xxr8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Law of Conservation of Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0l6999n",
      "content": "The law of conservation of energy states that energy can neither be created nor destroyed; it can only be converted from one form to another."
    },
    {
      "id": "cn6fhi3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Mechanical Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6woi6si",
      "content": "Mechanical energy is the sum of kinetic energy and potential energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tci49j7",
      "content": "Mechanical Energy = KE + PE"
    },
    {
      "id": "037za9e",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Meaning of Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "efvqv9v",
      "content": "Power is the rate at which work is done or energy is transferred."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ng23xno",
      "content": "Formula: Power = Work / Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1pjyxos",
      "content": "SI Unit of Power = Watt (W)"
    },
    {
      "id": "r29g6v2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Units of Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "If the velocity of a body is doubled, its Kinetic Energy increases four times (KE ∝ v²).",
        "1 Horsepower (HP) equals 746 Watts, a frequently asked conversion in competitive exams.",
        "The commercial unit of electricity is 1 kWh (kilowatt-hour), which equals 3.6 × 10⁶ Joules."
      ],
      "id": "sk04di1"
    },
